 "in_use_summary_en": "Kymenlaakso wellbeing services county says treatment recommendations for patients who cannot have surgery are made in its own multidisciplinary lung meeting, and that surgery decisions are made in Helsinki (Meilahti); no page says HUS joins that meeting by video or that every stage I–III patient is reviewed with HUS.",
 "missing_en": "No page shows a video review with the HUS surgeon, radiotherapy doctor and oncologist for every stage I–III patient before curative treatment is ruled out.",
 "summary_en": "Kymenlaakso wellbeing services county runs its own multidisciplinary lung meeting, which makes treatment recommendations when surgery is not possible; surgery decisions and operations happen at Meilahti hospital in Helsinki (HUS). HUS says its own lung specialist team gives recommendations when needed. No page shows a video review with HUS for every stage I–III patient. On effect, a single UK before-after study (2004) reported a 30% relative rise in resections, which supports the direction but not the size we assume.",
 "unanswered_en": "No page said whether HUS thoracic surgeons or oncologists take part in the Kymenlaakso lung meeting by video.",
